{"metric":"brans_dicke_sphere","source":[{"metric":"brans_dicke_sphere","system":"harmonic","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"04a445bdb9fe6603"},{"metric":"brans_dicke_sphere","system":"isotropic","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"c0811d8fdb38e9f6"},{"metric":"brans_dicke_sphere","system":"spherical","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"7caef494e05edf47"}],"views":[{"id":"isotropic","label":"Isotropic","box":[-0.35,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"isotropic","settings":"$C = -1/4$, $\\lambda = 1$, and $B = 1$, the unit of every length, so that $r_0 = 2B$, and $\\ell = 32B$; $p = \\arctan((ct - r_*)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + r_*)/\\ell)$.","caption":["The static sphere of Brans and Dicke's theory in Brans's isotropic radius $\\rho$ ($\\omega = 6$, $C = -1/4$, $\\lambda = 1$), each point in the diagram a 2-sphere. On the plane of $t$ and $\\rho$ the metric is $h^{2/\\lambda}(-c^2dt^2 + dr_*^2)$ with $h = (\\rho - B)/(\\rho + B)$ and $dr_*/d\\rho = h^{1 - (C + 2)/\\lambda}\\left(1 + B/\\rho\\right)^2$, and $r_*$ vanishes at $\\rho = B$, so $p = \\arctan((ct - r_*)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + r_*)/\\ell)$ bring the spacetime into Minkowski's triangle, drawn with $T = p + q$ up and $X = q - p$ across.","The edge $X = 0$ is $\\rho = B$, where the spheres have zero area and the Kretschmann scalar diverges: a timelike singularity with no horizon, so light leaving it reaches $\\mathscr{I}^+$. At $C = 0$ the isotropic radius of Schwarzschild's metric runs on through $\\rho = B$ into a second exterior, and at the values drawn the spacetime ends there."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","poi