[0.0,0.25],"text":"$\\rho = B$","anchor":"r","class":"lab","dx":-6,"dy":0},{"at":[1.7568,0.0],"text":"$\\rho = 8B$","anchor":"b","class":"coord","dx":0,"dy":-3}],"legend":[["fill","cover","the whole spacetime, which $t$ and $\\rho$ cover"],["line","r","$\\rho$ constant, at $1.05\\,B$, $1.5\\,B$, $2B$, $4B$, $8B$, $16B$, and $32B$"],["line","t","$ct$ constant, every $16B$ to $\\pm 32B$, and at $\\pm 64B$"],["zig","singular","the singularity $\\rho = B$, where the spheres have zero area and the Kretschmann scalar diverges"],["line","scri","null infinity $\\mathscr{I}^\\pm$"]],"slices":[{"view":"equator","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0$","version":"20094a833515d376","lines":[[[0.0995,0.0],[1.9412,0.0]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.9412,0.0],"anchor":"tr","dx":0,"dy":1.3}}]},{"id":"spherical","label":"Spherical","box":[-0.35,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"spherical","settings":"$m = 0$, $n = 1/4$, and $r_0 = 1$, the unit of every length, and $\\ell = 16r_0$; $p = \\arctan((ct - r_*)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + r_*)/\\ell)$.","caption":["The static sphere of Brans and Dicke's theory ($m = 0$, $n = 1/4$, which is $\\omega = 6$), each point in the diagram a 2-sphere of radius $rA^{n/2}$. On the plane of $t$ and $r$ the metric is $A^{m+1}(-c^2dt^2 + dr_*^2)$ with $A = 1 - 2r_0/r$ and $dr_*/dr = A^{-(m - n + 2)/2}$, and $r_*$ vanishes at $r = 2r_0$, so $p = \\arctan((ct - r_*)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + r_*)/\\ell)$ bring the spacetime into Minkowski's triangle, drawn with $T = p + q$ up and $X = q - p$ across.","The edge $X = 0$ is $r = 2r_0$, where the spheres have zero area and the Kretschmann scalar diverges: a timelike singularity with no horizon, so light leaving it reaches $\\mathscr{I}^+$. The triangle is Fisher's, whose metric is this one multiplied by the scalar field, a factor that moves no light ray. The strip between the edge and the first line drawn is the last thousandth of $r_0$ before the singularity, which light takes $6.2\\,r_0/c$ to cross: the power of $A$ in $dr_*/dr$ is $7/8$ where Schwarzschild's is $1$, and at $m = n = 0$ the integral for $r_*$ diverges at $r = 2r_0$, which is then Schwarzschild's horizon."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0,-3.1337],[0.0074,-2.9461],[0.0283,-2.7558],[0.0644,-2.5527],[0.1154,-2.34],[0.1657,-2.165],[0.2303,-1.9642],[0.4584,-1.3206],[0.5428,-1.0709],[0.6085,-0.8532],[0.6552,-0.6718],[0.6932,-0.4882],[0.7178,-0.3257],[0.7332,-0.1586],[0.738,0.002],[0.7327,0.1656],[0.7178,0.3257],[0.6932,0.4882],[0.6552,0.6718],[0.6085,0.8532],[0.5428,1.0709],[0.4584,1.3206],[0.2303,1.9642],[0.1657,2.165],[0.1154,2.34],[0.0644,2.5527],[0.0283,2.7558],[0.0074,2.9461],[0.0,3.1337]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0,-3.1337],[0.0034,-3.0429],[0.0123,-2.9525],[0.027,-2.86],[0.0476,-2.7651],[0.0726,-2.6733],[0.1028,-2.5797],[0.1445,-2.4674],[0.1884,-2.3621],[0.2757,-2.1751],[0.37,-1.9921],[0.482,-1.7877],[0.7513,-1.3109],[0.8799,-1.0724],[0.9956,-0.8362],[1.0752,-0.6477],[1.1377,-0.4648],[1.1771,-0.3084],[1.2013,-0.1528],[1.2093,-0.0015],[1.2073,0.0765],[1.2013,0.1528],[1.1771,0.3084],[1.1377,0.4648],[1.0752,0.6477],[0.9956,0.8362],[0.8799,1.0724],[0.7513,1.3109],[0.482,1.7877],[0.37,1.9921],[0.2757,2.1751],[0.1884,2.3621],[0.1445,2.4674],[0.1028,2.5797],[0.0726,2.6733],[0.0476,2.7651],[0.027,2.86],[0.0123,2.9525],[0.0034,3.0429],[0.0,3.1337]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0,-3.1337],[0.0036,-3.0497],[0.0133,-2.9653],[0.0293,-2.8785],[0.0519,-2.7888],[0.0796,-2.701],[0.1133,-2.6105],[0.1607,-2.5004],[0.2113,-2.3952],[0.3143,-2.2043],[0.4284,-2.0122],[0.5667,-1.7929],[0.9008,-1.2774],[1.0556,-1.0265],[1.1735,-0.8177],[1.2682,-0.626],[1.3347,-0.4622],[1.3611,-0.3829],[1.3855,-0.2941],[1.4019,-0.2171],[1.4127,-0.1467],[1.4197,-0.0721],[1.4219,-0.0013],[1.4197,0.0721],[1.4127,0.1467],[1.4